1
00:01:32,690 --> 00:01:35,030
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,229 --> 00:01:37,690
[Episode 13]

3
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:48,210
Chief, you wanted to see me?

4
00:01:50,710 --> 00:01:52,590
This case has had a huge impact.

5
00:01:53,070 --> 00:01:55,330
Rumors have been running rampant lately

6
00:01:55,350 --> 00:01:56,810
that a gang of murderers is

7
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:59,150
specifically targeting women
who are alone.

8
00:01:59,150 --> 00:02:00,120
It's gotten so bad
that young female workers

9
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,040
won't dare go to or from work

10
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:03,070
without a family member escorting them.

11
00:02:03,070 --> 00:02:05,230
Tell me, how much time are you giving us?

12
00:02:05,230 --> 00:02:05,960
Twenty days,

13
00:02:06,350 --> 00:02:08,680
starting from the day
the body was discovered.

14
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:09,410
Twenty days?

15
00:02:12,310 --> 00:02:14,250
Then we only have about 10 days left.

16
00:02:14,250 --> 00:02:16,000
The problem is,
we still haven't even confirmed

17
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,400
the identity of the body.

18
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:19,920
Didn't someone already identify the body?

19
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:21,630
Yes. That old lady

20
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:22,910
did insist

21
00:02:23,030 --> 00:02:24,760
it was her daughter, Yu Sanhua.

22
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:26,470
But her second daughter has

23
00:02:26,470 --> 00:02:28,200
never been sure that it was her.

24
00:02:30,870 --> 00:02:32,030
Do we have any suspects?

25
00:02:32,030 --> 00:02:32,430
Yes.

26
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:35,470
Yu Sanhua's husband,

27
00:02:35,470 --> 00:02:36,400
Qian Xingliang.

28
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:37,840
He had both the opportunity

29
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:38,710
and the motive.

30
00:02:39,240 --> 00:02:41,300
And he also approached the villagers

31
00:02:41,590 --> 00:02:42,750
to get their stories straight.

32
00:02:42,750 --> 00:02:43,310
Ergui,

33
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:44,710
um...

34
00:02:45,630 --> 00:02:46,560
do me a favor.

35
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:47,890
Sure. What is it?

36
00:02:52,750 --> 00:02:53,800
If anyone asks

37
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,400
whether we were

38
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:57,870
playing cards together 10 days ago,

39
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:59,310
just say we were,

40
00:02:59,910 --> 00:03:00,310
okay?

41
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:01,150
Sure.

42
00:03:01,870 --> 00:03:02,270
But...

43
00:03:02,630 --> 00:03:03,150
Why?

44
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:04,770
A couple of days ago,

45
00:03:04,770 --> 00:03:05,360
didn't they pull a body

46
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,470
out of the river?

47
00:03:06,780 --> 00:03:07,870
The police came to me today

48
00:03:07,870 --> 00:03:09,680
and questioned me for quite a while.

49
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:11,030
Do they suspect me?

50
00:03:11,750 --> 00:03:13,430
I'm afraid I'll be falsely accused.

51
00:03:13,430 --> 00:03:15,080
We did play cards together
around that time.

52
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:16,120
We did,

53
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:18,150
but I'm still nervous.

54
00:03:18,910 --> 00:03:19,310
Okay.

55
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:20,840
Put it on my tab.

56
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:22,970
I'll pay you back when I win some money.

57
00:03:23,030 --> 00:03:24,760
Why aren't you kids going home?

58
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:35,430
Ergui,

59
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:36,960
let's talk?

60
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:38,310
Me?

61
00:03:38,630 --> 00:03:38,960
Yes.

62
00:03:44,750 --> 00:03:46,300
Captain Liu, he's destroying evidence!

63
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:47,360
What are you doing?

64
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:48,760
Get up!

65
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:50,000
Come here!

66
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:51,310
Why are you arresting me?

67
00:03:51,310 --> 00:03:52,280
I didn't do anything!

68
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:53,430
Why are you arresting me?

69
00:03:53,430 --> 00:03:54,630
-Qian Xingliang!
-Don't move!

70
00:03:54,630 --> 00:03:55,829
Whose jacket is this?

71
00:03:56,030 --> 00:03:58,400
M-My wife's.

72
00:03:58,750 --> 00:04:00,280
Then why are you burning it?

73
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:02,470
I'm angry. I hated her.

74
00:04:02,630 --> 00:04:03,910
Is this the jacket she was wearing

75
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:05,240
when she came to see you?

76
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:08,680
She forgot to take it with her!

77
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:10,080
Didn't you say she never came?

78
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,430
She came into the house first,

79
00:04:11,430 --> 00:04:12,870
and then we went outside!

80
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:14,550
Take him away.

81
00:04:14,550 --> 00:04:15,890
No, I didn't kill her!

82
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:19,060
How do you know she's dead?

83
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:21,430
Wasn't the body from the river

84
00:04:21,430 --> 00:04:22,190
hers?

85
00:04:25,630 --> 00:04:26,830
We don't even know

86
00:04:26,830 --> 00:04:27,870
who the body is.

87
00:04:29,430 --> 00:04:30,290
How do you know?

88
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:35,630
Hasn't it already been confirmed?

89
00:04:35,630 --> 00:04:37,670
Not 100% confirmed.

90
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:39,680
Look, it states clearly there,

91
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:40,960
"basically consistent,"

92
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:43,270
but there are some discrepancies
in certain areas.

93
00:04:43,270 --> 00:04:45,200
You expect it to be a perfect match?

94
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:46,830
The head had been soaking in the water

95
00:04:46,830 --> 00:04:48,080
for who knows how many days.

96
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:48,870
I think we must be cautious

97
00:04:48,870 --> 00:04:50,400
-about this case.
-Enough!

98
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:52,390
Step up the interrogation.

99
00:04:52,390 --> 00:04:54,790
We must break Qian Xingliang
within 3 days.

100
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:57,000
You said you lured Yu Sanhua

101
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,870
into the woods by the river.

102
00:04:59,950 --> 00:05:00,630
Then what?

103
00:05:01,510 --> 00:05:02,480
I begged her...

104
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:04,430
not to leave.

105
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:06,750
She refused.

106
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:08,560
So I strangled her.

107
00:05:13,870 --> 00:05:14,800
Strangled her?

108
00:05:15,510 --> 00:05:17,240
Are you sure you strangled her?

109
00:05:19,430 --> 00:05:21,430
I took a knife and hacked at her head.

110
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:22,630
Her head?

111
00:05:22,750 --> 00:05:23,630
Neck.

112
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:24,830
Go on.

113
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:29,720
Mei. These are your cases.

114
00:05:30,630 --> 00:05:31,490
Put them there.

115
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:34,180
All the ones
everyone else passed on, right?

116
00:05:34,310 --> 00:05:35,560
Mei, don't overthink it.

117
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:37,159
The cases are assigned randomly
every time.

118
00:05:37,159 --> 00:05:37,950
This time, the chief judge

119
00:05:37,950 --> 00:05:38,800
specifically gave you

120
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:39,400
a big case.

121
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:40,390
What case?

122
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:43,960
Qian Xingliang's
intentional homicide case.

123
00:05:44,270 --> 00:05:44,870
Let me see.

124
00:05:49,510 --> 00:05:50,240
Xia,

125
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:51,900
you're really lucky.

126
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,130
You got a big case right from the start.

127
00:05:54,430 --> 00:05:55,750
With you leading us, Mei,

128
00:05:55,750 --> 00:05:57,080
we'll handle this well.

129
00:05:58,070 --> 00:05:59,070
It was really Xiaoguang who called

130
00:05:59,070 --> 00:06:00,200
and asked me to come.

131
00:06:00,310 --> 00:06:01,370
When I went inside,

132
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:03,630
that girl had already been made drunk

133
00:06:03,630 --> 00:06:04,830
and had no clothes on.

134
00:06:05,630 --> 00:06:06,800
I wanted to leave right away,

135
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:08,190
but Xiaoguang wouldn't let me.

136
00:06:08,190 --> 00:06:08,560
I...

137
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:10,640
So I didn't dare to leave.

138
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:13,240
Later, they all had their way with her.

139
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:13,560
I...

140
00:06:14,830 --> 00:06:15,680
So I did it too.

141
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:17,720
Talk about your own actions.

142
00:06:17,870 --> 00:06:19,040
Don't push everything

143
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:20,000
onto others.

144
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,020
Really, Presiding Judge.

145
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:24,720
I couldn't refuse.

146
00:06:25,510 --> 00:06:27,070
Xiaoguang did it on purpose.

147
00:06:27,070 --> 00:06:28,240
Mentor, ask him

148
00:06:28,270 --> 00:06:29,720
whether Xiaoguang showed any signs

149
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:31,050
of mental abnormality,

150
00:06:31,160 --> 00:06:32,270
like being overly excited,

151
00:06:32,270 --> 00:06:33,510
speaking incoherently, or such.

152
00:06:33,510 --> 00:06:34,159
Ask him.

153
00:06:34,870 --> 00:06:36,380
I'd say you look pretty excited

154
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:37,510
right now.

155
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:50,620
You just had to force me to adjourn, huh?

156
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:51,330
Had to make

157
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:52,890
a big scene out of this, huh?

158
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:55,800
Calm down, Mentor.

159
00:07:00,070 --> 00:07:00,830
If Song Xiaoguang

160
00:07:00,830 --> 00:07:02,090
is really mentally ill

161
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,650
and has mania on top of that,

162
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:04,560
then he must've

163
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:05,410
shown abnormal behaviors.

164
00:07:05,410 --> 00:07:07,000
How could he
have been perfectly fine normally,

165
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:07,620
only to suddenly become

166
00:07:07,620 --> 00:07:09,270
mentally ill after the crime?

167
00:07:09,270 --> 00:07:10,160
And none of his many accomplices

168
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:11,220
noticed anything?

169
00:07:13,190 --> 00:07:13,870
Don't you know

170
00:07:13,870 --> 00:07:15,310
there's such a thing as
intermittent episodes?

171
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:16,700
What kind of "episode" just happens to

172
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:18,960
flare up every time he assaults someone?

173
00:07:19,530 --> 00:07:20,680
You know more than psychiatrist experts,

174
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:21,310
do you?

175
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:22,800
That evaluation report

176
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:24,530
bears the signatures of 5 psychiatrists

177
00:07:24,530 --> 00:07:25,770
here in Binjiang,

178
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,230
all stamped with official seals!

179
00:07:27,230 --> 00:07:28,750
They're all wrong,
and you're the only one who's right?

180
00:07:28,750 --> 00:07:29,800
I never said I was right.

181
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:32,750
I just want to request
another psychiatric evaluation.

182
00:07:32,750 --> 00:07:34,150
You make it sound so easy.

183
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:36,040
Do you think the people
behind Song Xiaoguang

184
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,159
wouldn't understand what you're after?

185
00:07:37,159 --> 00:07:37,870
Why do you always mention

186
00:07:37,870 --> 00:07:39,070
the people behind him? You...

187
00:07:39,070 --> 00:07:40,930
You're out of line, you know that?

188
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:47,400
Hello, this is Zhang Deshan.

189
00:07:49,070 --> 00:07:49,730
Court Pres.

190
00:07:58,070 --> 00:07:58,730
Okay, okay.

191
00:07:59,190 --> 00:07:59,950
I understand. I understand.

192
00:07:59,950 --> 00:08:00,550
Don't go!

193
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:02,200
Come back!

194
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:03,290
Don't worry.

195
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:04,940
I'll... I'll handle it.

196
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:06,000
Alright, alright.

197
00:08:06,510 --> 00:08:07,970
Come back. Close the door!

198
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:16,160
Sit!

199
00:08:20,510 --> 00:08:22,240
You really have a mind of your own,

200
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:24,240
going to a psychiatric hospital
to investigate secretly?

201
00:08:24,240 --> 00:08:25,240
It wasn't secret.

202
00:08:25,510 --> 00:08:26,560
I went there openly.

203
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:27,830
Openly? Then why didn't you

204
00:08:27,830 --> 00:08:28,960
tell me beforehand?

205
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:31,240
People might think

206
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:32,360
I put you up to it!

207
00:08:32,390 --> 00:08:33,500
Did I put you up to it?

208
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:34,700
Keep your voice down.

209
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:38,630
No.

210
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:41,400
You really don't think things through.

211
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:42,600
Mentor, does our court

212
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:43,380
not even have the right

213
00:08:43,380 --> 00:08:44,780
to investigate anymore?

214
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:45,510
What rules did I violate

215
00:08:45,510 --> 00:08:46,270
by checking out the patient

216
00:08:46,270 --> 00:08:46,750
at

217
00:08:46,750 --> 00:08:47,570
the psychiatric hospital?

218
00:08:47,570 --> 00:08:49,570
I didn't say you violated any rules.

219
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:50,150
I mean...

220
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,240
Before you do something,

221
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:55,100
could you think it through first?

222
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:57,790
Anyone can act on impulse.

223
00:08:57,790 --> 00:08:58,250
Mentor.

224
00:08:59,750 --> 00:09:01,610
Can you really stomach that thug?

225
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:03,320
Just let that bastard

226
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:05,180
play us for fools with that paper?

227
00:09:09,390 --> 00:09:10,450
I can't stomach it.

228
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:24,490
Gaoyuan,

229
00:09:25,390 --> 00:09:26,450
let me warn you now.

230
00:09:27,870 --> 00:09:28,390
If you

231
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:32,120
really intend to pursue this...

232
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:35,120
there is no turning back.

233
00:09:39,870 --> 00:09:41,330
What does that "hmm" mean?

234
00:09:41,910 --> 00:09:42,960
Have you come around

235
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:44,090
or made up your mind?

236
00:09:44,540 --> 00:09:45,270
"Hmm" again?

237
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:46,390
Say something.

238
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:51,350
You're beyond my control.

239
00:09:51,350 --> 00:09:52,510
Go see the court president.

240
00:09:52,510 --> 00:09:53,440
I'm telling you,

241
00:09:53,670 --> 00:09:54,790
I'd rather be jerked around

242
00:09:54,790 --> 00:09:55,650
by my superiors

243
00:09:55,650 --> 00:09:57,050
than be played for a fool

244
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:58,280
over a piece of paper!

245
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,400
You're driving me crazy.

246
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:12,000
I'm sorry, Mentor.

247
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,400
I think you're my mentor!

248
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:16,480
I should've told you beforehand

249
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:18,080
that I was going to
the psychiatric hospital.

250
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:19,610
Thank you for not telling me!

251
00:10:19,610 --> 00:10:21,540
And don't tell me next time either!

252
00:10:29,750 --> 00:10:30,810
Alright, alright.

253
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:32,970
Don't do this again.

254
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,260
I have no principles when it comes to you.

255
00:10:37,390 --> 00:10:38,550
Y-You... cut it out.

256
00:10:39,750 --> 00:10:41,080
Actually, this is nice.

257
00:10:43,030 --> 00:10:43,480
Xia,

258
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,120
I've thought about it!

259
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:46,810
This time we need to
plan things out carefully.

260
00:10:46,810 --> 00:10:48,070
Qian Xingliang's case

261
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:48,960
is a major one.

262
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:51,000
Let's try to get the trial
scheduled for the 1st.

263
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:51,840
We need to step it up

264
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:53,640
and show them what we're made of.

265
00:10:56,390 --> 00:10:56,910
Xia?

266
00:11:05,390 --> 00:11:05,790
Xia!

267
00:11:07,030 --> 00:11:08,320
Mei, I'm sorry.

268
00:11:09,380 --> 00:11:11,600
I said, let's try to get this case's trial

269
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:12,930
on the 1st of next month.

270
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:14,200
Go arrange it.

271
00:11:15,150 --> 00:11:15,720
Mei,

272
00:11:16,070 --> 00:11:18,120
I suggest we don't rush to trial.

273
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:21,770
What do you mean?

274
00:11:22,560 --> 00:11:23,550
I think there are still

275
00:11:23,550 --> 00:11:25,220
a lot of problems with this case.

276
00:11:25,220 --> 00:11:26,600
How come I didn't see any problems?

277
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:27,440
You've read the file, right?

278
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:28,370
Of course I have.

279
00:11:28,570 --> 00:11:29,600
The basic facts are clear,

280
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:30,870
and the basic evidence is solid.

281
00:11:30,870 --> 00:11:33,000
That's exactly where the problem lies:

282
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,800
"basic" doesn't mean complete.

283
00:11:40,270 --> 00:11:41,510
No wonder you're a top law student

284
00:11:41,510 --> 00:11:43,310
from a prestigious university—

285
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:44,770
so picky about wording.

286
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:46,630
Fine, tell me then—

287
00:11:46,870 --> 00:11:48,870
where do you think the problems lie?

288
00:11:49,630 --> 00:11:50,150
Look.

289
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:52,510
The police found 3 body parts

290
00:11:52,510 --> 00:11:54,000
in 3 different locations

291
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:55,510
and barely managed to piece them together

292
00:11:55,510 --> 00:11:56,710
into one female body.

293
00:11:57,030 --> 00:11:58,840
But because the body
was severely decomposed,

294
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:00,870
it was impossible to
identify the deceased.

295
00:12:00,870 --> 00:12:01,200
Okay.

296
00:12:01,590 --> 00:12:02,390
Then, 3 days later,

297
00:12:02,390 --> 00:12:03,910
they still hadn't identified the body.

298
00:12:03,910 --> 00:12:05,090
So the police issued a public notice

299
00:12:05,090 --> 00:12:06,090
asking for information.

300
00:12:06,090 --> 00:12:07,120
The day after that notice

301
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:07,780
was issued,

302
00:12:08,030 --> 00:12:09,600
Qian Xingliang's mother-in-law—

303
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:10,510
that is the mother

304
00:12:10,510 --> 00:12:11,520
of the deceased—

305
00:12:11,550 --> 00:12:12,630
came to the police station.

306
00:12:12,630 --> 00:12:13,550
She insisted

307
00:12:13,550 --> 00:12:14,330
that the body

308
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:15,960
was her daughter, Yu Sanhua.

309
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:17,000
So,

310
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:18,080
Qian Xingliang

311
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:19,340
is the murder suspect.

312
00:12:21,030 --> 00:12:21,440
Yes.

313
00:12:21,670 --> 00:12:22,960
He is under suspicion.

314
00:12:24,390 --> 00:12:25,240
But...

315
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:28,670
Come on, but what?

316
00:12:30,510 --> 00:12:32,600
I have serious doubts about
whether the deceased

317
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:33,930
was actually Yu Sanhua.

318
00:12:38,550 --> 00:12:38,960
Yu.

319
00:12:44,630 --> 00:12:45,120
Yu!

320
00:12:45,910 --> 00:12:46,570
Court Pres.

321
00:12:48,310 --> 00:12:49,150
Need me for something?

322
00:12:49,150 --> 00:12:49,510
No.

323
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:52,140
I-I was just passing by. You carry on.

324
00:13:11,910 --> 00:13:12,710
Zhang Deshan,

325
00:13:13,550 --> 00:13:14,390
why did you send that kid

326
00:13:14,390 --> 00:13:15,440
over to me?

327
00:13:15,670 --> 00:13:16,730
You're pretty sly.

328
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:18,810
Court Pres.,

329
00:13:19,190 --> 00:13:20,000
we can't just stand by

330
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:20,750
and let that bunch

331
00:13:20,750 --> 00:13:22,080
climb all over us, can we?

332
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:23,480
And rub our noses in it too.

333
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:24,480
Even I can't do anything.

334
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:26,240
What can that apprentice of yours do?

335
00:13:26,240 --> 00:13:28,360
Let's release the wild card first.

336
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:29,840
Whether he can turn things upside down

337
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:31,390
depends on his luck.

338
00:13:32,150 --> 00:13:35,340
But I'm the one who'll have to
clean up the mess afterward.

339
00:13:35,340 --> 00:13:36,840
I'd like to help you clean it up,

340
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:38,550
but I don't have that big a mop.

341
00:13:43,550 --> 00:13:45,360
Zhang Deshan, you brat.

342
00:13:49,630 --> 00:13:50,670
What makes you think

343
00:13:50,670 --> 00:13:52,240
that the badly decomposed body

344
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:53,370
wasn't Yu Sanhua's?

345
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:54,670
It's not that I believe it wasn't—

346
00:13:54,670 --> 00:13:55,930
it's that I don't know.

347
00:13:57,910 --> 00:13:58,910
I thought you had

348
00:13:58,910 --> 00:13:59,970
some new evidence.

349
00:14:01,510 --> 00:14:02,000
Mei,

350
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:04,340
sometimes acknowledging
what you don't know

351
00:14:04,340 --> 00:14:05,600
can bring you closer to the truth

352
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:07,400
than assuming you already know.

353
00:14:07,870 --> 00:14:09,530
You're quite philosophical.

354
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:11,360
Look.

355
00:14:11,870 --> 00:14:13,870
This is the police forensic report.

356
00:14:13,890 --> 00:14:14,440
Even they aren't

357
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:15,440
100% certain

358
00:14:15,510 --> 00:14:17,310
that the deceased was Yu Sanhua.

359
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:20,790
It's my daughter.

360
00:14:23,510 --> 00:14:25,200
Erhua, what do you think?

361
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:29,960
It seems... seems like her...

362
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:33,640
It seems like my third sister...

363
00:14:33,670 --> 00:14:34,730
Can you be certain?

364
00:14:39,510 --> 00:14:40,240
Captain Liu.

365
00:14:45,270 --> 00:14:47,030
This is the craniofacial superimposition

366
00:14:47,030 --> 00:14:47,790
report.

367
00:14:48,350 --> 00:14:49,520
The conclusion states

368
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:50,590
"highly similar."

369
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:52,480
It's not a definitive confirmation.

370
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:54,270
But wasn't the body identified twice?

371
00:14:54,270 --> 00:14:55,930
Yes, it was identified twice.

372
00:14:56,030 --> 00:14:56,960
The first time was based on

373
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:58,620
a reconstructed facial image

374
00:14:58,670 --> 00:15:00,150
created from the badly decomposed body.

375
00:15:00,150 --> 00:15:01,750
That method isn't particularly accurate.

376
00:15:01,750 --> 00:15:02,610
The second time

377
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:03,840
was based on

378
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,320
craniofacial superimposition
using the skull.

379
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:06,750
Look.

380
00:15:07,410 --> 00:15:08,200
This image

381
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:09,800
shows 70-80%

382
00:15:09,910 --> 00:15:11,440
similarity to her actual photo.

383
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:12,520
But both times,

384
00:15:12,550 --> 00:15:14,030
family members identified the body

385
00:15:14,030 --> 00:15:14,830
and confirmed

386
00:15:14,910 --> 00:15:16,440
it was Yu Sanhua herself.

387
00:15:16,510 --> 00:15:18,310
And that is the biggest problem.

388
00:15:18,630 --> 00:15:19,630
Look at these 2 photos.

389
00:15:19,630 --> 00:15:21,390
They're actually quite different,

390
00:15:21,390 --> 00:15:22,870
yet they insist the photos look like her.

391
00:15:22,870 --> 00:15:24,320
Isn't that easy to understand?

392
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:25,600
A mother desperate to
identify her daughter.

393
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:26,120
Besides,

394
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:27,120
the body had been soaking in water

395
00:15:27,120 --> 00:15:28,120
for many days,

396
00:15:28,390 --> 00:15:29,030
so some deformation

397
00:15:29,030 --> 00:15:30,290
is entirely possible.

398
00:15:31,870 --> 00:15:33,600
There is another possibility—

399
00:15:34,630 --> 00:15:36,890
the deceased may not have been Yu Sanhua.

400
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:42,800
You're being far too subjective.

401
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:45,030
The family's identification doesn't count,

402
00:15:45,030 --> 00:15:46,480
craniofacial superimposition
doesn't count—

403
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:48,010
then you tell me, what does?

404
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:50,840
Actually, the most reliable method

405
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:52,600
is the skull superimposition appraisal.

406
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:54,270
They did the skull superimposition.

407
00:15:54,270 --> 00:15:55,270
Look at the report

408
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:56,030
yourself—

409
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:57,700
"basically consistent."

410
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:03,560
"Basically" isn't good enough, right?

411
00:16:03,670 --> 00:16:04,540
You just said

412
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:06,400
"basic" doesn't mean complete.

413
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:08,120
Right.

414
00:16:08,510 --> 00:16:09,670
The report states

415
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:12,480
there are slight discrepancies
in two areas.

416
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:13,480
That suggests it's possible

417
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:15,210
the deceased was not Yu Sanhua.

418
00:16:18,810 --> 00:16:19,320
Even if there's only

419
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:20,510
a 1% possibility,

420
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,060
we can't make a hasty determination.

421
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:26,200
So after all that,

422
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:28,150
the skull comparison
isn't good enough either.

423
00:16:28,150 --> 00:16:29,510
That doesn't count either.

424
00:16:29,510 --> 00:16:30,270
Then what?

425
00:16:30,550 --> 00:16:32,270
Nothing counts unless you say it?

426
00:16:32,270 --> 00:16:34,440
It's not that I get to decide
what counts, Mei.

427
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:34,750
I just think...

428
00:16:34,750 --> 00:16:35,480
Xia.

429
00:16:35,510 --> 00:16:36,360
How about this?

430
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,820
You go tell the chief judge

431
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:39,440
that you will hear this case!

432
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:40,680
You be the presiding judge,

433
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:42,210
and I'll be your assistant!

434
00:16:43,870 --> 00:16:44,240
Mei.

435
00:16:53,790 --> 00:16:54,590
What's wrong?

436
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:56,680
It has nothing to do with you.

437
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:59,190
Are you free after work?
I want to talk to you.

438
00:16:59,190 --> 00:17:00,670
Work matter or personal matter?

439
00:17:00,670 --> 00:17:02,600
If it's work stuff, let's talk now.

440
00:17:02,910 --> 00:17:03,510
Personal.

441
00:17:12,450 --> 00:17:14,210
S-Slow down.

442
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:15,170
You're rushing.

443
00:17:15,589 --> 00:17:17,000
One moment you say I'm too slow,

444
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:18,109
and the next you say I'm too fast.

445
00:17:18,109 --> 00:17:20,240
How exactly do you want me to make them?

446
00:17:20,240 --> 00:17:21,270
L-Look at you.

447
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:23,160
You're rolling out the wrapper so thick.

448
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:24,829
When these dumplings are cooked,

449
00:17:24,829 --> 00:17:25,869
the wrappers will be tough.

450
00:17:25,869 --> 00:17:27,200
Lihui has a weak stomach.

451
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:29,050
How is she supposed to digest that?

452
00:17:29,050 --> 00:17:29,880
Anyone who didn't know better

453
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:31,800
would think you were cooking
for a labor camp.

454
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:32,640
Now I get it.

455
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:33,890
In this house, Lihui

456
00:17:34,440 --> 00:17:35,370
is not my student

457
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:36,980
but your own daughter.

458
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:38,860
You're clearly favoring her.

459
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:42,350
Lihui! Answer the phone.

460
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:44,100
Both of us have our hands full.

461
00:17:46,310 --> 00:17:47,620
Hello, this is Zhou Yipu's residence.

462
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:48,860
Hello, this is Chen Yizhong.

463
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:50,860
Could you please get Mr. Zhou for me?

464
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:51,770
Yizhong,

465
00:17:52,510 --> 00:17:53,370
it's me, Lihui.

466
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:54,450
Zhang Lihui?

467
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Why are you there?

468
00:17:56,430 --> 00:17:58,350
I haven't heard your voice in a long time.

469
00:17:58,350 --> 00:17:59,350
How have you been?

470
00:18:00,160 --> 00:18:01,880
I'm fine. How about you?

471
00:18:02,350 --> 00:18:02,790
I...

472
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:04,770
W-Which aspect do you mean?

473
00:18:06,510 --> 00:18:07,440
Which aspect...

474
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:09,020
Health, of course.

475
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:11,940
I've lost some weight.

476
00:18:12,750 --> 00:18:13,550
Why?

477
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,070
Are you under too much stress,

478
00:18:15,070 --> 00:18:16,530
or are you feeling unwell?

479
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:17,960
Chen Yizhong,

480
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:20,000
you never used to fuss this much.

481
00:18:21,510 --> 00:18:22,200
I know.

482
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:24,030
You're just showing concern for me.

483
00:18:24,030 --> 00:18:24,630
Thank you.

484
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:29,410
It's been, what,

485
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,330
several years since we last spoke, right?

486
00:18:32,830 --> 00:18:35,030
Are you still in touch with Xia Yingjie?

487
00:18:36,350 --> 00:18:38,240
Well, you're looking for Mr. Zhou, right?

488
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:39,370
I'll get him for you.

489
00:18:39,940 --> 00:18:40,850
Mr. Zhou!

490
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:41,960
Yizhong is on the phone!

491
00:18:41,960 --> 00:18:42,560
Yizhong?

492
00:18:42,590 --> 00:18:43,630
I'll go answer it.

493
00:18:44,460 --> 00:18:45,110
You go roll out the wrappers.

494
00:18:45,110 --> 00:18:45,840
Give it to me.

495
00:18:47,350 --> 00:18:48,270
Come on, give it to me. Give it to me.

496
00:18:48,270 --> 00:18:49,200
Hello, Yizhong.

497
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:52,400
You wrap it.

498
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:53,200
I'll help you.

499
00:18:58,480 --> 00:19:00,860
[Conference Room 2]

500
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:00,960
My supervisor
didn't give any advice either.

501
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:02,480
Do you think it's feasible?

502
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:03,350
I've only heard

503
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:05,830
a brief overview of the case from you.

504
00:19:05,830 --> 00:19:07,690
So it's not appropriate for me...

505
00:19:08,350 --> 00:19:10,410
to give a specific opinion on sentencing.

506
00:19:10,410 --> 00:19:11,350
You should discuss that

507
00:19:11,350 --> 00:19:12,610
with your supervisor.

508
00:19:12,790 --> 00:19:14,120
But I have to remind you:

509
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:17,000
the NPC's provision
permitting harsher sentences

510
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,240
beyond the statutory range

511
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:19,310
for serious crimes

512
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:21,310
was a policy holdover

513
00:19:21,310 --> 00:19:23,110
from the Strike-Hard Campaign.

514
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:24,960
Although it hasn't been
completely repealed,

515
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:26,110
it's rarely been applied

516
00:19:26,110 --> 00:19:27,170
over the past year.

517
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:29,880
This is exactly what my mentor

518
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:30,640
said.

519
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,270
But it can still be applied,

520
00:19:33,270 --> 00:19:33,670
right?

521
00:19:35,110 --> 00:19:36,870
The fact that it's rarely applied

522
00:19:36,870 --> 00:19:38,400
doesn't mean
the situations in which it applies

523
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:39,830
have objectively decreased.

524
00:19:39,830 --> 00:19:41,270
Rather, more and more judges

525
00:19:41,270 --> 00:19:42,550
have come to understand, subjectively,

526
00:19:42,550 --> 00:19:44,310
that sentencing must be handled carefully.

527
00:19:44,310 --> 00:19:47,080
We can't keep imposing excessive sentences
the way we did

528
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:49,310
at the beginning of
the Strike-Hard Campaign.

529
00:19:49,310 --> 00:19:50,000
I think

530
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:52,330
this reflects progress

531
00:19:52,550 --> 00:19:54,550
in people's awareness of the rule of law

532
00:19:54,550 --> 00:19:57,210
as well as progress
in China's judicial system.

533
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:00,440
I understand.

534
00:20:00,830 --> 00:20:02,270
But actually, the circumstances

535
00:20:02,270 --> 00:20:04,410
of this case are especially egregious.

536
00:20:04,410 --> 00:20:05,480
It's had a major impact

537
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:07,030
throughout the entire city.

538
00:20:07,030 --> 00:20:07,880
That's why I was thinking about

539
00:20:07,880 --> 00:20:10,210
whether it should be dealt with severely.

540
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:12,830
Yizhong,

541
00:20:14,550 --> 00:20:16,480
convincing me isn't what matters.

542
00:20:17,030 --> 00:20:17,920
What matters

543
00:20:19,030 --> 00:20:20,430
is convincing yourself.

544
00:20:21,110 --> 00:20:23,440
If you were already firm in your decision,

545
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:26,030
you wouldn't have made this call,

546
00:20:26,030 --> 00:20:26,510
right?

547
00:20:29,550 --> 00:20:30,880
I understand, Mr. Zhou.

548
00:20:31,750 --> 00:20:32,430
Thank you.

549
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:34,070
Take care of yourself.

550
00:20:34,070 --> 00:20:35,530
I'll wait to hear from you.

551
00:20:41,590 --> 00:20:42,920
So, basically,

552
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:44,530
Song Xiaoguang was the ringleader

553
00:20:44,530 --> 00:20:46,050
of this gang of 11.

554
00:20:46,610 --> 00:20:47,690
But he's not on

555
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:48,850
the defendant list.

556
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:50,240
He's got himself a psychiatric certificate

557
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:51,550
and is hiding out
in a psychiatric hospital.

558
00:20:51,550 --> 00:20:52,680
Yes, that's basically it.

559
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:53,680
What do you think?

560
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:55,540
Send the case back.

561
00:20:56,030 --> 00:20:58,110
Make the procuratorate explain itself

562
00:20:58,110 --> 00:21:01,040
and request a review
of the psychiatric evaluation.

563
00:21:01,350 --> 00:21:02,880
What are you planning to do?

564
00:21:03,970 --> 00:21:04,920
That's exactly what I'm thinking of doing.

565
00:21:04,920 --> 00:21:05,440
But you...

566
00:21:05,440 --> 00:21:06,700
But you've been going back and forth,

567
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:08,160
agonizing over it, right?

568
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:11,590
We've got some reservations,
at least a little, right?

569
00:21:11,590 --> 00:21:13,590
I can't just act recklessly, right?

570
00:21:15,350 --> 00:21:17,350
Being timid isn't the same as
being cautious,

571
00:21:17,350 --> 00:21:18,750
just as being blunt

572
00:21:18,750 --> 00:21:20,950
isn't the same as being reckless, okay?

573
00:21:23,160 --> 00:21:25,160
It's been a long time
since you roasted me like this.

574
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:26,620
I'm actually quite happy.

575
00:21:27,240 --> 00:21:28,040
Are you crazy?

576
00:21:29,510 --> 00:21:30,970
Then why did you come to me?

577
00:21:31,070 --> 00:21:31,830
To complain?

578
00:21:32,550 --> 00:21:33,480
I'm not exactly the best person

579
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:34,310
to vent to.

580
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:36,220
No, I just wanted to chat with you.

581
00:21:37,160 --> 00:21:38,220
You know my mentor.

582
00:21:38,310 --> 00:21:39,640
He's always the one trying to

583
00:21:39,640 --> 00:21:40,770
smooth things over,

584
00:21:41,080 --> 00:21:41,730
but he

585
00:21:41,750 --> 00:21:44,010
still wants to put that jerk behind bars.

586
00:21:45,030 --> 00:21:45,840
He's an old hand in the court.

587
00:21:45,840 --> 00:21:46,680
He's worked for a long time

588
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:47,880
and has got a lot of tricks up his sleeve.

589
00:21:47,880 --> 00:21:48,550
Lately, he's been pulling them on me,

590
00:21:48,550 --> 00:21:49,880
asking me to go to the court president.

591
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:50,400
Did you?

592
00:21:51,070 --> 00:21:51,720
I did.

593
00:21:51,750 --> 00:21:53,590
But right at the door, I hesitated.

594
00:21:53,590 --> 00:21:56,050
You're always weighing every little thing.

595
00:21:56,720 --> 00:21:57,720
I think our court has a very strong

596
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:58,660
sense of integrity.

597
00:21:58,660 --> 00:22:00,070
You can go directly to
the court president.

598
00:22:00,070 --> 00:22:01,130
He'll support you.

599
00:22:01,510 --> 00:22:03,400
If I just go directly to
the court president like that,

600
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:04,440
wouldn't I be dumping the pressure

601
00:22:04,440 --> 00:22:05,030
of making the decision onto him?

602
00:22:05,030 --> 00:22:06,000
I'd just be the one
who opens the can of worms.

603
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:07,060
T-T-That would...

604
00:22:07,240 --> 00:22:08,760
That would be too inappropriate.

605
00:22:08,760 --> 00:22:09,790
Well, what's wrong with
just opening the can of worms?

606
00:22:09,790 --> 00:22:10,610
Opening the can of worms also requires

607
00:22:10,610 --> 00:22:11,480
a lot of courage.

608
00:22:11,480 --> 00:22:12,420
Courage alone isn't enough.

609
00:22:12,420 --> 00:22:13,620
You also need wisdom.

610
00:22:14,160 --> 00:22:15,270
Are you taking a shot at me?

611
00:22:15,270 --> 00:22:17,000
No, I'm not.

612
00:22:17,030 --> 00:22:18,440
I mean, for example,

613
00:22:18,880 --> 00:22:19,400
suppose we come up with

614
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:20,310
a good solution,

615
00:22:20,310 --> 00:22:20,710
right?

616
00:22:20,830 --> 00:22:21,830
And this solution

617
00:22:22,030 --> 00:22:23,550
could not only bring that rich kid

618
00:22:23,550 --> 00:22:24,160
to justice

619
00:22:24,510 --> 00:22:26,350
but also spare the court president some,

620
00:22:26,350 --> 00:22:27,200
or even all,

621
00:22:27,240 --> 00:22:28,070
of the pressure from above.

622
00:22:28,070 --> 00:22:29,750
Wouldn't that be a job well done?

623
00:22:29,750 --> 00:22:30,150
Right?

624
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:31,750
Then the odds of success would go up,

625
00:22:31,750 --> 00:22:32,640
the court president would get to see

626
00:22:32,640 --> 00:22:33,310
how capable I am,

627
00:22:33,310 --> 00:22:35,440
and we'd uphold judicial justice
in the process.

628
00:22:35,440 --> 00:22:36,770
How great would that be?

629
00:22:36,930 --> 00:22:37,680
You're really not subtle about

630
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:38,880
wanting it all.

631
00:22:39,220 --> 00:22:39,960
No, I can't just

632
00:22:39,960 --> 00:22:41,110
go in headfirst, right?

633
00:22:41,110 --> 00:22:42,310
That would be so stupid.

634
00:22:42,310 --> 00:22:42,750
So?

635
00:22:43,510 --> 00:22:44,640
What can I do for you?

636
00:22:44,840 --> 00:22:45,590
I just wanted to ask you

637
00:22:45,590 --> 00:22:47,590
if you could think of a way to do this.

638
00:22:48,790 --> 00:22:50,320
Anyway, my stance is that

639
00:22:50,350 --> 00:22:51,680
whether or not you have

640
00:22:51,720 --> 00:22:52,350
this so-called solution,

641
00:22:52,350 --> 00:22:54,680
you can still go directly to
the court president.

642
00:22:54,680 --> 00:22:56,010
Bring out your courage.

643
00:22:56,030 --> 00:22:57,690
Where did all your courage go?

644
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:01,480
What does this have to do with...

645
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:06,930
What happened between you and Mei?

646
00:23:12,160 --> 00:23:13,760
I don't want to talk about it.

647
00:23:14,720 --> 00:23:15,220
You're leaving?

648
00:23:15,220 --> 00:23:15,640
Bye.

649
00:23:18,920 --> 00:23:20,590
Don't always give me

650
00:23:20,590 --> 00:23:22,190
t-that sour look from now on.

651
00:23:30,750 --> 00:23:31,200
Hello.

652
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:33,880
Dad.

653
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:35,510
Yizhong.

654
00:23:36,350 --> 00:23:37,480
Yizhong's calling?

655
00:23:38,110 --> 00:23:40,240
Do you remember, when I was a kid,

656
00:23:41,640 --> 00:23:42,310
they humiliated my mom

657
00:23:42,310 --> 00:23:44,570
by hanging the "loose woman" sign on her?

658
00:23:48,680 --> 00:23:50,790
Why are you suddenly calling

659
00:23:50,790 --> 00:23:51,790
to ask about that?

660
00:23:53,130 --> 00:23:53,860
I want to ask—

661
00:23:53,920 --> 00:23:55,120
if something similar

662
00:23:55,240 --> 00:23:56,920
happened now,

663
00:23:58,270 --> 00:24:00,240
a group of people
publicly humiliating a woman,

664
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:02,900
and the methods used
were even more despicable,

665
00:24:03,270 --> 00:24:04,510
the circumstances even more severe...

666
00:24:04,510 --> 00:24:07,110
There won't be another "if"
like that anymore.

667
00:24:07,920 --> 00:24:08,590
Our country

668
00:24:09,120 --> 00:24:10,770
has paid such a heavy price

669
00:24:10,830 --> 00:24:12,490
and taken so many wrong turns,

670
00:24:13,070 --> 00:24:14,000
just to prevent

671
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:15,930
such things from happening again.

672
00:24:17,110 --> 00:24:18,790
W-What exactly are you trying to say?

673
00:24:18,790 --> 00:24:20,310
What if it did happen now?

674
00:24:21,750 --> 00:24:22,950
As a presiding judge,

675
00:24:23,440 --> 00:24:24,500
how would you rule?

676
00:24:25,270 --> 00:24:27,200
I'm not a presiding judge anymore.

677
00:24:27,480 --> 00:24:28,270
Right now,

678
00:24:28,780 --> 00:24:30,100
I'm just an archivist

679
00:24:30,120 --> 00:24:30,930
who needs help

680
00:24:30,960 --> 00:24:32,200
going up the stairs.

681
00:24:33,110 --> 00:24:34,240
I can't answer

682
00:24:34,240 --> 00:24:35,100
that question.

683
00:24:35,890 --> 00:24:37,200
B-Because neither the me now,

684
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:38,350
nor the me back then,

685
00:24:38,960 --> 00:24:40,400
is you.

686
00:24:43,070 --> 00:24:43,870
I understand.

687
00:24:44,160 --> 00:24:44,690
Yizhong,

688
00:24:44,700 --> 00:24:46,150
I-I have to remind you.

689
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:48,000
As a prosecutor,

690
00:24:48,960 --> 00:24:50,880
you cannot let your personal experiences

691
00:24:50,880 --> 00:24:52,480
or your anger control you.

692
00:24:53,680 --> 00:24:55,140
You must remain rational.

693
00:24:55,410 --> 00:24:56,070
I'm not being controlled

694
00:24:56,070 --> 00:24:56,990
by my past experiences.

695
00:24:56,990 --> 00:24:58,650
Then what do you want me to say?

696
00:24:59,350 --> 00:25:00,030
Do you want me to encourage you

697
00:25:00,030 --> 00:25:01,680
to use your prosecutorial power

698
00:25:01,680 --> 00:25:02,940
to punish those people

699
00:25:03,110 --> 00:25:03,870
as severely

700
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:05,480
and as quickly as possible?

701
00:25:05,480 --> 00:25:06,960
Would that make you happy?

702
00:25:09,960 --> 00:25:11,020
I'm hanging up now.

703
00:25:24,790 --> 00:25:27,030
Come on, help me taste this.

704
00:25:27,200 --> 00:25:29,480
Is the soup seasoned right?

705
00:25:36,270 --> 00:25:36,920
Is it?

706
00:25:37,920 --> 00:25:38,440
Yes.

707
00:25:46,790 --> 00:25:48,590
Comrade, please show me your ID.

708
00:26:03,510 --> 00:26:03,920
Quick.

709
00:26:05,350 --> 00:26:05,900
Go!

710
00:26:15,510 --> 00:26:16,750
Defend, defend!

711
00:26:18,720 --> 00:26:19,720
Speed up! Faster!

712
00:26:20,310 --> 00:26:22,110
Or I'll make you do shuttle runs!

713
00:26:24,030 --> 00:26:24,430
Quick.

714
00:26:29,830 --> 00:26:31,160
You must be Fang Haohao.

715
00:26:31,830 --> 00:26:33,270
You're the one from the court?

716
00:26:33,270 --> 00:26:33,590
Yes.

717
00:26:33,920 --> 00:26:35,520
Yu Gaoyuan. Nice to meet you.

718
00:26:37,920 --> 00:26:39,980
Uncle, watch out for the basketball!

719
00:26:44,310 --> 00:26:45,160
Be careful!

720
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:52,600
Thank you.

721
00:26:53,200 --> 00:26:55,030
Honestly, I reached out
to a lot of people,

722
00:26:55,030 --> 00:26:57,360
but you're the only one
willing to meet me.

723
00:27:00,030 --> 00:27:02,290
I'll keep a record of this conversation.

724
00:27:11,490 --> 00:27:12,110
Why didn't you call ahead

725
00:27:12,110 --> 00:27:13,480
to set up a time?

726
00:27:13,590 --> 00:27:15,990
I just strolled over
during my lunch break.

727
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:17,000
Besides, who are you

728
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:19,060
that I'd need to book an appointment?

729
00:27:19,510 --> 00:27:20,000
Forget it then.

730
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:20,830
No, no, no.

731
00:27:21,110 --> 00:27:23,170
Let's go have some noodles. Let's go.

732
00:27:24,020 --> 00:27:25,220
What a temper.

733
00:27:25,270 --> 00:27:26,270
I can't say a word.

734
00:27:28,400 --> 00:27:30,200
I was in the same class as him
from kindergarten

735
00:27:30,200 --> 00:27:31,540
all the way through high school.

736
00:27:31,540 --> 00:27:32,510
If he's mentally ill,

737
00:27:32,510 --> 00:27:34,970
shouldn't I be considered
mentally ill too?

738
00:27:36,080 --> 00:27:37,350
Could you describe those issues

739
00:27:37,350 --> 00:27:39,110
a little more objectively?

740
00:27:41,070 --> 00:27:42,110
You have absolutely

741
00:27:42,110 --> 00:27:43,110
no sense of humor.

742
00:27:44,220 --> 00:27:44,640
Okay.

743
00:27:45,350 --> 00:27:46,750
I'll put it objectively.

744
00:27:47,160 --> 00:27:48,960
Song Xiaoguang is not mentally ill.

745
00:27:48,960 --> 00:27:50,290
He's perfectly normal.

746
00:27:53,550 --> 00:27:54,020
Of course,

747
00:27:54,020 --> 00:27:55,270
that's only based on what I observed.

748
00:27:55,270 --> 00:27:56,400
I'm no doctor.

749
00:27:59,200 --> 00:27:59,800
Thank you.

750
00:28:00,640 --> 00:28:02,160
What you've provided

751
00:28:02,240 --> 00:28:03,100
is very useful.

752
00:28:03,200 --> 00:28:04,330
I know what to do now.

753
00:28:07,680 --> 00:28:08,750
Isn't investigation supposed to be

754
00:28:08,750 --> 00:28:10,070
the job of the police

755
00:28:10,070 --> 00:28:11,400
and the procuratorate?

756
00:28:11,510 --> 00:28:13,770
Why are you out here doing this yourself?

757
00:28:13,830 --> 00:28:14,510
You seem to know quite a lot

758
00:28:14,510 --> 00:28:15,770
about our line of work.

759
00:28:16,750 --> 00:28:18,510
I interned
at the Intermediate Court before

760
00:28:18,510 --> 00:28:19,970
but didn't end up joining.

761
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:20,700
Really?

762
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:23,070
What a pity.

763
00:28:23,270 --> 00:28:23,930
If you had,

764
00:28:23,960 --> 00:28:25,620
we could've been colleagues.

765
00:28:27,400 --> 00:28:28,270
You really know how to sweet-talk people.

766
00:28:28,270 --> 00:28:28,750
No.

767
00:28:28,920 --> 00:28:30,920
I-I'm really not just being polite.

768
00:28:31,750 --> 00:28:32,830
I think you're...

769
00:28:33,750 --> 00:28:35,410
straightforward and candid.

770
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:36,880
You have a sense of humor.

771
00:28:36,880 --> 00:28:38,310
And I can tell that you're

772
00:28:38,590 --> 00:28:39,650
a very kind person.

773
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:44,360
You really remind me of
a former female classmate of mine.

774
00:28:44,750 --> 00:28:45,880
I'm not like anyone.

775
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:51,000
I'm sorry.

776
00:28:53,400 --> 00:28:54,200
Just kidding.

777
00:28:56,310 --> 00:28:59,310
You're pushing so hard
to get Song Xiaoguang arrested.

778
00:28:59,310 --> 00:29:00,590
Do your higher-ups agree?

779
00:29:00,590 --> 00:29:02,190
It must be difficult, right?

780
00:29:02,920 --> 00:29:03,720
It's not easy.

781
00:29:06,070 --> 00:29:07,330
He should be arrested.

782
00:29:08,750 --> 00:29:11,160
He should've gotten his retribution
a long time ago.

783
00:29:11,160 --> 00:29:12,720
Just because you think

784
00:29:12,750 --> 00:29:14,830
the deceased might not be Yu Sanhua,

785
00:29:15,480 --> 00:29:17,140
you want to send the case back?

786
00:29:18,960 --> 00:29:20,420
That's what I'm thinking.

787
00:29:21,070 --> 00:29:22,470
But there's resistance.

788
00:29:22,590 --> 00:29:24,240
Our team leader, Mei,

789
00:29:24,590 --> 00:29:25,280
disagrees.

790
00:29:26,350 --> 00:29:27,610
What's her reasoning?

791
00:29:27,640 --> 00:29:28,920
She thinks...

792
00:29:30,240 --> 00:29:32,270
It'll sound like I'm reducing
her reasoning to pure self-interest,

793
00:29:32,270 --> 00:29:34,310
but I think
that's exactly what's going on.

794
00:29:34,310 --> 00:29:35,640
Because over the years,

795
00:29:35,640 --> 00:29:36,770
this is the first major case

796
00:29:36,770 --> 00:29:37,730
she's handled.

797
00:29:38,200 --> 00:29:40,400
She couldn't bear to send the case back.

798
00:29:42,400 --> 00:29:43,270
Sorry, Mei.

799
00:29:43,960 --> 00:29:46,820
I'm really not speaking ill of you
behind your back.

800
00:29:48,310 --> 00:29:49,970
Well, I am speaking ill of you.

801
00:29:53,350 --> 00:29:54,350
Well,

802
00:29:54,350 --> 00:29:55,880
if she absolutely refuses,

803
00:29:56,000 --> 00:29:56,930
what will you do?

804
00:29:58,440 --> 00:30:00,440
Isn't that what I'm worrying about?

805
00:30:00,830 --> 00:30:02,760
Mei is really not easy to deal with.

806
00:30:03,650 --> 00:30:04,960
It's as if my expressing
a different opinion

807
00:30:04,960 --> 00:30:06,760
were like slowly poisoning her.

808
00:30:09,030 --> 00:30:10,240
I miss my mentor.

809
00:30:11,310 --> 00:30:13,440
If it were her handling this...

810
00:30:14,160 --> 00:30:16,820
Who at our procuratorate
is handling this case?

811
00:30:17,720 --> 00:30:18,650
What do you want?

812
00:30:18,880 --> 00:30:20,010
Don't get involved.

813
00:30:20,030 --> 00:30:21,070
Can't I just ask?

814
00:30:21,270 --> 00:30:22,000
Stop asking.

815
00:30:24,070 --> 00:30:25,590
Anyway, I won't let this matter

816
00:30:25,590 --> 00:30:27,720
go without getting to the bottom of it.

817
00:30:27,830 --> 00:30:29,560
After all, 3 lives are at stake.

818
00:30:30,720 --> 00:30:31,550
I believe you.

819
00:30:32,430 --> 00:30:33,110
Otherwise, you wouldn't be

820
00:30:33,110 --> 00:30:33,840
Xia Yingjie.

821
00:30:36,510 --> 00:30:38,570
You're not from around here, are you?

822
00:30:38,750 --> 00:30:40,030
No. How could you tell?

823
00:30:41,640 --> 00:30:43,970
I'm from a rural area in another province.

824
00:30:44,590 --> 00:30:45,590
I studied in Beijing,

825
00:30:45,590 --> 00:30:46,310
and after graduation,

826
00:30:46,310 --> 00:30:47,440
I was assigned here.

827
00:30:48,240 --> 00:30:48,840
No wonder.

828
00:30:50,030 --> 00:30:50,890
No wonder what?

829
00:30:51,450 --> 00:30:52,720
No wonder you're so recklessly brave.

830
00:30:52,720 --> 00:30:54,450
You've got guts. I admire that.

831
00:30:55,880 --> 00:30:57,210
Good luck, college boy.

832
00:31:01,310 --> 00:31:03,000
Let me ask you one last question.

833
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:04,400
You don't have to answer.

834
00:31:05,510 --> 00:31:06,970
That's quite the buildup.

835
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:07,530
Go ahead.

836
00:31:09,830 --> 00:31:10,650
Did he...

837
00:31:11,200 --> 00:31:12,930
By "he," I mean Song Xiaoguang.

838
00:31:13,790 --> 00:31:15,960
Did he ever try to...

839
00:31:15,960 --> 00:31:16,960
or even want to...

840
00:31:17,960 --> 00:31:18,510
hurt you?

841
00:31:20,680 --> 00:31:21,680
He wouldn't dare.

842
00:31:21,960 --> 00:31:23,830
He wouldn't dare, not in a million years.

843
00:31:23,830 --> 00:31:26,160
My dad would never let him
get away with it.

844
00:31:26,720 --> 00:31:27,450
That's good.

845
00:31:32,590 --> 00:31:34,590
Well, it's not that he never hurt me.

846
00:31:35,070 --> 00:31:36,400
Just in a different way.

847
00:31:38,960 --> 00:31:40,160
He gave me a nickname.

848
00:31:40,830 --> 00:31:42,160
He called me "Miss Limp."

849
00:31:42,160 --> 00:31:43,750
This nickname followed me
from kindergarten

850
00:31:43,750 --> 00:31:45,550
all the way through high school.

851
00:31:49,480 --> 00:31:50,440
Now do you know why I agreed to

852
00:31:50,440 --> 00:31:51,240
meet you?

853
00:31:51,260 --> 00:31:51,790
I know.

854
00:31:54,510 --> 00:31:55,770
He should be arrested.

855
00:31:55,890 --> 00:31:56,480
Uncle,

856
00:31:56,480 --> 00:31:58,080
come play with us for a while!

857
00:31:58,200 --> 00:31:58,550
Sure.

858
00:31:59,310 --> 00:32:00,880
They're just tired from playing.

859
00:32:00,880 --> 00:32:01,960
I'll play with them for a bit.

860
00:32:01,960 --> 00:32:02,420
Come on.

861
00:32:03,310 --> 00:32:03,770
Come on!

862
00:32:08,830 --> 00:32:09,440
Come on!

863
00:32:11,200 --> 00:32:12,880
Over there, over there, over there!

864
00:32:12,880 --> 00:32:14,080
Pass the basketball!

865
00:32:15,030 --> 00:32:15,690
Great play!

866
00:32:50,070 --> 00:32:51,750
I've spent this whole time
talking about myself.

867
00:32:51,750 --> 00:32:53,070
Why did you want to see me?

868
00:32:53,070 --> 00:32:55,070
It can't have been just for noodles.

869
00:32:57,440 --> 00:32:59,240
Just for noodles. Nothing else.

870
00:33:00,790 --> 00:33:01,520
Impossible.

871
00:33:02,510 --> 00:33:02,970
Tell me.

872
00:33:05,270 --> 00:33:06,270
Really, nothing.

873
00:33:08,200 --> 00:33:09,030
There's nothing about my cases

874
00:33:09,030 --> 00:33:10,230
worth talking about.

875
00:33:12,310 --> 00:33:13,440
Not telling me, huh?

876
00:33:13,920 --> 00:33:14,920
I'm leaving then.

877
00:33:15,170 --> 00:33:16,110
A couple of days ago, I called

878
00:33:16,110 --> 00:33:17,030
Mr. Zhou.

879
00:33:17,920 --> 00:33:19,180
Zhang Lihui answered.

880
00:33:19,880 --> 00:33:21,610
I know what you're going to say.

881
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:24,000
She's doing well.

882
00:33:24,400 --> 00:33:26,130
Things are good between us too.

883
00:33:28,270 --> 00:33:29,730
Thank you for the noodles.

884
00:33:29,830 --> 00:33:31,480
And thank you
for listening to my complaints,

885
00:33:31,480 --> 00:33:33,340
for being someone I could talk to.

886
00:33:36,030 --> 00:33:36,490
I'm off.

887
00:33:40,590 --> 00:33:41,510
I'm actually pretty happy about

888
00:33:41,510 --> 00:33:43,170
being someone you can talk to.

889
00:33:46,680 --> 00:33:48,200
Thank you, Chen Yizhong.

890
00:34:02,160 --> 00:34:02,960
Zhang,

891
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:05,720
I guarantee you've never

892
00:34:05,920 --> 00:34:07,580
had this kind of apple before.

893
00:34:08,110 --> 00:34:09,960
This is from Aksu,

894
00:34:09,960 --> 00:34:10,840
Xinjiang.

895
00:34:11,360 --> 00:34:12,000
Zhiguo's

896
00:34:12,030 --> 00:34:13,489
father's old subordinate

897
00:34:13,840 --> 00:34:15,800
specially sent someone to deliver them.

898
00:34:15,800 --> 00:34:17,000
Go on. Very sweet.

899
00:34:17,550 --> 00:34:18,210
Try a piece.

900
00:34:24,550 --> 00:34:25,210
Is it sweet?

901
00:34:26,320 --> 00:34:26,760
Yes.

902
00:34:27,250 --> 00:34:28,110
Let me tell you,

903
00:34:28,360 --> 00:34:30,360
your Deputy Chief Prosecutor Liang

904
00:34:30,400 --> 00:34:32,360
never praises people.

905
00:34:32,880 --> 00:34:34,710
But he's been praising you all along,

906
00:34:34,710 --> 00:34:37,110
saying you're quiet and sensible,

907
00:34:37,400 --> 00:34:39,730
that you graduated from a top university,

908
00:34:39,760 --> 00:34:42,560
and that you're Mr. Zhou's
postgraduate student.

909
00:34:42,880 --> 00:34:44,520
Even though it's part-time,

910
00:34:44,550 --> 00:34:46,480
that's still no easy achievement.

911
00:34:46,800 --> 00:34:48,080
Everyone knows

912
00:34:48,120 --> 00:34:50,040
Mr. Zhou is one of the country's

913
00:34:50,070 --> 00:34:52,920
leading experts in criminal law.

914
00:34:53,760 --> 00:34:55,670
His judgment can't be wrong.

915
00:34:56,760 --> 00:34:57,670
I took Mr. Zhou's courses

916
00:34:57,670 --> 00:34:59,270
when I was an undergraduate.

917
00:35:01,190 --> 00:35:02,480
Let me tell you, before

918
00:35:02,510 --> 00:35:03,510
Deputy Chief Prosecutor Liang

919
00:35:03,510 --> 00:35:04,770
introduced Zhiguo...

920
00:35:05,630 --> 00:35:06,960
I won't hide it from you.

921
00:35:06,960 --> 00:35:07,960
He introduced Zhiguo

922
00:35:07,960 --> 00:35:09,190
to several girls,

923
00:35:09,480 --> 00:35:10,760
but none of them were any good.

924
00:35:10,760 --> 00:35:12,560
None of them made the cut with me.

925
00:35:13,110 --> 00:35:14,600
But you're different from them.

926
00:35:14,600 --> 00:35:15,290
Even though

927
00:35:15,320 --> 00:35:17,120
this is the first time we've met,

928
00:35:17,480 --> 00:35:18,680
I'm pleased with you.

929
00:35:18,840 --> 00:35:19,500
You passed.

930
00:35:19,960 --> 00:35:21,670
A child with a background like yours,

931
00:35:21,670 --> 00:35:22,930
all alone in the world—

932
00:35:23,180 --> 00:35:24,880
even after being assigned to the SPP,

933
00:35:24,880 --> 00:35:25,760
you're still

934
00:35:25,760 --> 00:35:27,150
just an ordinary official.

935
00:35:27,150 --> 00:35:28,410
If you want to advance,

936
00:35:28,800 --> 00:35:31,060
you need someone to pull strings for you.

937
00:35:33,440 --> 00:35:35,000
Our Zhiguo is different.

938
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:36,710
Zhiguo is at the SPC.

939
00:35:37,000 --> 00:35:38,550
He's young and capable.

940
00:35:38,550 --> 00:35:39,840
His superiors think highly of him,

941
00:35:39,840 --> 00:35:41,640
so he has a lot of room to advance.

942
00:35:42,110 --> 00:35:44,110
If you two get married,

943
00:35:44,360 --> 00:35:46,020
your life will be much easier.

944
00:35:48,630 --> 00:35:49,070
Mom.

945
00:35:50,810 --> 00:35:52,070
Lihui is finishing her master's degree

946
00:35:52,070 --> 00:35:52,690
this year.

947
00:35:53,840 --> 00:35:55,510
A master's degree?

948
00:35:55,510 --> 00:35:56,530
What's the big deal?

949
00:35:56,530 --> 00:35:59,060
Isn't that very common
in the procuratorate?

950
00:35:59,720 --> 00:36:00,810
I just want to know—

951
00:36:00,840 --> 00:36:02,710
what plans do you have

952
00:36:02,730 --> 00:36:03,450
for

953
00:36:03,800 --> 00:36:05,660
your future career and your life?

954
00:36:06,960 --> 00:36:08,280
My plan is

955
00:36:08,590 --> 00:36:10,510
to work at the grassroots level
and gain experience.

956
00:36:10,510 --> 00:36:11,240
That's good.

957
00:36:11,670 --> 00:36:12,480
Young people

958
00:36:12,510 --> 00:36:14,710
should get more practical experience.

959
00:36:15,110 --> 00:36:15,550
Yes.

960
00:36:16,040 --> 00:36:17,590
I'm planning to apply for
a grassroots procuratorate position

961
00:36:17,590 --> 00:36:18,440
in Xijiang.

962
00:36:31,800 --> 00:36:33,200
The apple is quite sweet.

963
00:36:52,630 --> 00:36:54,510
Oh, you're just embarrassing.

964
00:36:56,710 --> 00:36:58,230
A hard-luck look, an even harder life—

965
00:36:58,230 --> 00:37:00,000
and no luck for her husband, either.

966
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:00,710
Vulgar.

967
00:37:03,400 --> 00:37:04,670
Who are you talking about?

968
00:37:04,670 --> 00:37:05,230
You...

969
00:37:07,360 --> 00:37:09,490
I don't even know what to say about you.

970
00:37:15,590 --> 00:37:16,550
Say that again.

971
00:37:18,550 --> 00:37:19,070
Lihui,

972
00:37:19,710 --> 00:37:20,800
I'm really sorry.

973
00:37:21,840 --> 00:37:23,170
My mom is just like that.

974
00:37:23,230 --> 00:37:24,480
I've told her many times,

975
00:37:24,480 --> 00:37:25,940
but she just won't change.

976
00:37:26,670 --> 00:37:27,600
I only came today

977
00:37:27,880 --> 00:37:29,630
because Prosecutor Liang meant well
by arranging this,

978
00:37:29,630 --> 00:37:31,290
and I could hardly refuse him.

979
00:37:31,590 --> 00:37:33,920
I'll just think of it
as a work assignment.

980
00:37:38,710 --> 00:37:39,190
Lihui.

981
00:37:42,190 --> 00:37:43,320
I really like you.

982
00:37:44,800 --> 00:37:47,530
Otherwise, I wouldn't have asked
Uncle Liang...

983
00:37:49,480 --> 00:37:50,890
It's really my fault today.

984
00:37:50,890 --> 00:37:51,820
I was too abrupt.

985
00:37:51,920 --> 00:37:53,380
It's okay. Don't say that.

986
00:37:53,710 --> 00:37:54,440
I don't mind.

987
00:37:55,280 --> 00:37:56,940
So you shouldn't mind either.

988
00:37:57,150 --> 00:37:57,880
I'm leaving.

989
00:37:58,960 --> 00:37:59,490
So...

990
00:38:01,550 --> 00:38:03,960
What you said earlier
about going to Xijiang—

991
00:38:03,960 --> 00:38:04,890
is that for real,

992
00:38:05,360 --> 00:38:07,420
or are you just trying to scare my mom?

993
00:38:08,760 --> 00:38:10,420
Is Xijiang really that scary?

994
00:38:24,280 --> 00:38:25,920
There are 5 confessions in total.

995
00:38:25,920 --> 00:38:27,070
You can see a gradual process
of the account

996
00:38:27,070 --> 00:38:28,920
moving closer to the established facts.

997
00:38:28,920 --> 00:38:30,800
The defendant first confessed

998
00:38:30,890 --> 00:38:32,320
a week after being detained.

999
00:38:32,320 --> 00:38:32,960
At first,

1000
00:38:33,000 --> 00:38:34,440
the time, location, and method of killing

1001
00:38:34,440 --> 00:38:34,960
didn't match up at all.

1002
00:38:34,960 --> 00:38:35,560
Thank you.

1003
00:38:35,630 --> 00:38:36,030
Hello.

1004
00:38:37,960 --> 00:38:40,150
Only later did his statements
gradually begin to line up.

1005
00:38:40,150 --> 00:38:41,950
These two, and a serving of rice.

1006
00:38:42,590 --> 00:38:44,150
Isn't that perfectly normal?

1007
00:38:44,150 --> 00:38:45,480
He didn't want to admit it at first

1008
00:38:45,480 --> 00:38:46,680
but later came clean.

1009
00:38:48,320 --> 00:38:49,190
I think we can't rule out

1010
00:38:49,190 --> 00:38:51,520
the possibility of a coerced confession.

1011
00:38:52,710 --> 00:38:54,240
Isn't there another piece of evidence?

1012
00:38:54,240 --> 00:38:55,110
The bloodstain found on the knife

1013
00:38:55,110 --> 00:38:56,360
at Qian Xingliang's home.

1014
00:38:56,360 --> 00:38:57,480
The blood type of that stain

1015
00:38:57,480 --> 00:38:58,800
matches Yu Sanhua's.

1016
00:38:58,970 --> 00:38:59,880
And Yu Sanhua's blood type

1017
00:38:59,880 --> 00:39:01,010
matches the body's.

1018
00:39:01,560 --> 00:39:02,670
But blood type alone

1019
00:39:02,670 --> 00:39:03,920
cannot establish that the bloodstain

1020
00:39:03,920 --> 00:39:04,670
belonged to Yu Sanhua.

1021
00:39:04,670 --> 00:39:06,000
Lots of people share the same blood type.

1022
00:39:06,000 --> 00:39:06,690
That doesn't prove

1023
00:39:06,690 --> 00:39:08,000
that Yu Sanhua was the deceased.

1024
00:39:08,000 --> 00:39:10,400
Wouldn't that be
too much of a coincidence?

1025
00:39:15,280 --> 00:39:17,490
What kind of dish is this?
So much fatty meat.

1026
00:39:17,490 --> 00:39:18,290
I said no meat,

1027
00:39:18,320 --> 00:39:19,250
yet they still gave me so much fatty meat.

1028
00:39:19,250 --> 00:39:20,850
How am I supposed to eat this?

1029
00:39:27,960 --> 00:39:28,440
Get in.

1030
00:39:45,070 --> 00:39:46,400
Qian Xingliang, right?

1031
00:39:47,710 --> 00:39:48,230
I'm the lawyer

1032
00:39:48,230 --> 00:39:50,430
assigned to you by the bar association.

1033
00:39:50,440 --> 00:39:51,440
My name is Tan Xin.

1034
00:39:53,710 --> 00:39:54,310
Sign here.

1035
00:39:58,530 --> 00:39:59,260
Do I...

1036
00:40:01,030 --> 00:40:02,160
have to pay for this?

1037
00:40:03,320 --> 00:40:04,050
Just sign it.

1038
00:40:04,510 --> 00:40:05,670
You don't have to pay.

1039
00:40:05,670 --> 00:40:07,470
The government covers the cost.

1040
00:40:16,190 --> 00:40:17,050
Give me the pen.

1041
00:40:17,070 --> 00:40:18,600
Press it right on your name.

1042
00:40:21,190 --> 00:40:21,920
There you go.

1043
00:40:23,670 --> 00:40:24,600
Qian Xingliang,

1044
00:40:24,920 --> 00:40:26,180
did you kill your wife?

1045
00:40:26,230 --> 00:40:26,670
I did.

1046
00:40:28,510 --> 00:40:29,150
I didn't.

1047
00:40:29,550 --> 00:40:30,550
I didn't kill her.

1048
00:40:30,590 --> 00:40:31,760
You scared me for a second.

1049
00:40:31,760 --> 00:40:32,290
Alright,

1050
00:40:32,430 --> 00:40:33,630
then tell me about it.

1051
00:40:33,840 --> 00:40:34,640
Tell you what?

1052
00:40:38,800 --> 00:40:40,860
How much money does your family have?

1053
00:40:41,920 --> 00:40:43,840
The bloodstain was found
in Qian Xingliang's home

1054
00:40:43,840 --> 00:40:45,280
15 days after the crime.

1055
00:40:45,550 --> 00:40:47,070
If that really was the victim's blood,

1056
00:40:47,070 --> 00:40:48,070
he just left it on the knife

1057
00:40:48,070 --> 00:40:48,920
all this time?

1058
00:40:49,230 --> 00:40:50,550
Does Qian Xingliang's household

1059
00:40:50,550 --> 00:40:52,410
only have that one kitchen knife?

1060
00:40:52,710 --> 00:40:53,320
Not sure.

1061
00:40:54,480 --> 00:40:55,940
The case file doesn't say.

1062
00:40:57,710 --> 00:40:59,400
It's possible that after killing her,

1063
00:40:59,400 --> 00:41:00,360
Qian Xingliang simply never used

1064
00:41:00,360 --> 00:41:02,020
that particular knife again.

1065
00:41:02,450 --> 00:41:02,810
Mei,

1066
00:41:02,840 --> 00:41:03,940
if I were the killer,

1067
00:41:03,940 --> 00:41:04,960
I definitely wouldn't keep

1068
00:41:04,960 --> 00:41:06,020
the murder weapon.

1069
00:41:06,070 --> 00:41:07,360
And why would I

1070
00:41:07,360 --> 00:41:08,090
be so attached to

1071
00:41:08,090 --> 00:41:09,320
a lousy kitchen knife like that?

1072
00:41:09,320 --> 00:41:10,110
Just leaving it there—

1073
00:41:10,110 --> 00:41:10,900
neither willing to use it

1074
00:41:10,900 --> 00:41:12,500
nor willing to throw it away.

1075
00:41:15,550 --> 00:41:17,760
Without money,
this is going to be hard to handle.

1076
00:41:17,760 --> 00:41:19,740
If you sell your house and land,

1077
00:41:19,880 --> 00:41:20,810
actively compensate the victim's family,

1078
00:41:20,810 --> 00:41:21,840
and try your best to

1079
00:41:21,840 --> 00:41:23,150
gain their forgiveness,

1080
00:41:23,150 --> 00:41:25,480
you might get a suspended death sentence.

1081
00:41:27,040 --> 00:41:28,920
Your case caused quite a sensation

1082
00:41:28,920 --> 00:41:30,180
in Binjiang back then.

1083
00:41:31,320 --> 00:41:31,850
Alright.

1084
00:41:32,280 --> 00:41:33,940
Anything else you want to say?

1085
00:41:33,960 --> 00:41:34,800
I'm innocent.

1086
00:41:35,800 --> 00:41:37,060
Tell me something new.

1087
00:41:37,190 --> 00:41:38,480
Counsel, I truly am innocent.

1088
00:41:38,480 --> 00:41:39,360
I didn't kill anyone...

1089
00:41:39,360 --> 00:41:40,190
Alright. This is enough.

1090
00:41:40,190 --> 00:41:41,590
I have other things to do.

1091
00:41:41,750 --> 00:41:42,960
I'll come see you again in a few days.

1092
00:41:42,960 --> 00:41:43,900
Take care of yourself

1093
00:41:43,900 --> 00:41:44,670
in here.

1094
00:41:45,480 --> 00:41:46,080
Oh, and...

1095
00:41:47,070 --> 00:41:47,670
eat

1096
00:41:48,400 --> 00:41:49,400
as much as you can.

1097
00:41:55,320 --> 00:41:55,710
Xia,

1098
00:41:56,630 --> 00:41:57,400
our disagreement on this case

1099
00:41:57,400 --> 00:41:59,060
is really quite significant.

1100
00:41:59,710 --> 00:42:00,190
Mei,

1101
00:42:00,960 --> 00:42:02,360
let's put all that aside.

1102
00:42:03,040 --> 00:42:04,680
The fundamental question is

1103
00:42:04,710 --> 00:42:06,880
whether the deceased really was Yu Sanhua.

1104
00:42:06,880 --> 00:42:08,110
If we got this wrong,

1105
00:42:08,110 --> 00:42:09,770
it would be a massive blunder.

1106
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:11,680
We would both be held responsible.

1107
00:42:11,680 --> 00:42:12,590
It could even end

1108
00:42:12,590 --> 00:42:13,630
our careers.

1109
00:42:14,480 --> 00:42:14,960
Mei,

1110
00:42:15,280 --> 00:42:17,340
I just don't want us to take that risk.

1111
00:42:18,280 --> 00:42:19,190
So,

1112
00:42:19,360 --> 00:42:21,220
you're doing this for my own good.

1113
00:42:21,410 --> 00:42:22,800
I thought that, even if you never said it,

1114
00:42:22,800 --> 00:42:23,940
deep down you thought I was too old,

1115
00:42:23,940 --> 00:42:24,920
that my professional skills
weren't up to par,

1116
00:42:24,920 --> 00:42:26,550
and that I couldn't keep up with
the times.

1117
00:42:26,550 --> 00:42:27,230
Thank you

1118
00:42:27,550 --> 00:42:28,810
for looking out for me.

1119
00:42:29,240 --> 00:42:30,880
Y-You're really overthinking it.

1120
00:42:30,880 --> 00:42:32,680
You're the one overthinking it.

1121
00:42:34,230 --> 00:42:35,160
Let me be direct.

1122
00:42:35,920 --> 00:42:36,590
I believe

1123
00:42:37,320 --> 00:42:38,720
the body was Yu Sanhua's.

1124
00:42:39,190 --> 00:42:40,480
There's no problem with that.

1125
00:42:40,480 --> 00:42:41,920
The evidence, the confession,

1126
00:42:41,920 --> 00:42:42,920
and the forensic reports

1127
00:42:42,920 --> 00:42:44,510
are all accepted
by the police and the procuratorate.

1128
00:42:44,510 --> 00:42:46,480
The possibility of an error
is extremely low.

1129
00:42:46,480 --> 00:42:48,710
The possibility
you're talking about exists,

1130
00:42:48,710 --> 00:42:49,880
but it's just a remote possibility.

1131
00:42:49,880 --> 00:42:52,560
But even the remotest possibility
could still happen.

1132
00:42:52,560 --> 00:42:53,890
This concerns 3 lives,

1133
00:42:53,920 --> 00:42:54,360
Mei.

1134
00:42:54,630 --> 00:42:55,880
How is that 3 lives?

1135
00:42:56,400 --> 00:42:57,510
If Qian Xingliang's convicted,

1136
00:42:57,510 --> 00:42:59,440
he'll definitely get the death penalty.

1137
00:42:59,440 --> 00:43:00,810
Then who exactly is the dead woman?

1138
00:43:00,810 --> 00:43:01,920
Is Yu Sanhua dead or alive?

1139
00:43:01,920 --> 00:43:03,030
We wouldn't know either of those.
